This directory contains a Python adaptation of algorithm components originally
published by Ali Ahrari in the AMLP-RS-CMSA-ESII MATLAB package (version 1.0,
2022). Those components and their adaptations are provided under the Creative
Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International license:

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode

Original code record and attribution:
https://www.researchgate.net/publication/362154784_AMLP-RS-CMSA-ESII
https://sites.google.com/view/evopt/award

The author's included notice states that the code may be used for
non-commercial and academic research, including funded academic research,
with acknowledgement and citation of the AMLP and improved RS-CMSA papers.
The source package's dmmops benchmark code is explicitly excluded from that
notice and has not been incorporated into this runtime implementation.

Changes in this adaptation (2026): Python/NumPy translation of the distributed
CMSA-ESII implementation and main.m defaults, EDOLAB maximization, notified
environment changes and bounded function-evaluation accounting. No CMA-ES
core reconstruction is used. Adaptations are enumerated in README.md.

Required references:
Ahrari et al. Adaptive multilevel prediction method for dynamic multimodal
optimization. IEEE TEVC 25(3):463-477, 2021. DOI:10.1109/TEVC.2021.3051172.
Ahrari et al. Static and dynamic multimodal optimization by improved covariance
matrix self-adaptation evolution strategy with repelling subpopulations.
IEEE TEVC 26(3):527-541, 2022. DOI:10.1109/TEVC.2021.3117116.
EvOpt Reports 2022002 and 2022003, University of New South Wales.
